    q: "My Telecaster Has A Maple Neck. Does That Make It A 1950s Guitar?",
    a: "Not on its own. Look at the back. A one-piece maple neck from the 1950s has to carry a dark walnut skunk stripe, because the truss rod went in from behind and the stripe caps the channel. The maple cap that came back in the late 1960s has a separate board glued over the rod, so the back is clean unbroken maple with no stripe. Same wood, same look from the playing side, and about a decade apart. The stripe returns for good in 1971 with the bullet truss rod.",
  },
