    q: "Why Does My Telecaster Have Two Capacitors In The Control Cavity?",
    a: "Because it is a Telecaster. The Tele ran a more involved circuit than the Stratocaster did, and from late 1952 the dark circuit put a flat rectangular phone book capacitor in alongside a round tubular one. Two caps in a Tele cavity is not a modified guitar. Check it against the wiring for its year rather than against a Strat, where one cap is normal.",
